From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:15:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: stop the background Windows read-ACL helper from
 holding its launchers' pipes open

The first elevated Windows sandbox setup starts a read-ACL helper that keeps running after setup returns. It
inherited every inheritable handle of the setup helper, including the sandbox wrapper's stderr pipe that the
exec-server reads. The exec-server's read of that pipe then did not end, and the pending blocking read kept
`codex-exec-server --listen stdio` from exiting after its stdin closed until the helper finished. The helper now
starts with no inherited handle except a NUL device for its standard I/O.
